## Worktree Routing

Read .github-project.json before creating a worktree. Use its worktreeRoot value and create one worktree per issue:

```sh
config=$(node -e 'const fs=require("fs"); const c=JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(".github-project.json")); console.log(JSON.stringify({worktreeRoot:c.worktreeRoot, documentation:c.documentation}, null, 2))'
git worktree add "__WORKTREE_ROOT__/__ISSUE_ID__" -b "__BRANCH_NAME__" "__BASE_BRANCH__"
```

Do not set core.worktree. Do not create a second project documentation tree in the repository.

